        "evidence": "hecke-satisfies-blitvic-hypothesis-proof.md:7-9 claims sigma_i* = sigma_i (self-adjoint) 'since tr_M(sigma_i)=tr_M(sigma_i^-1)=z'.",
        "notes": "Trace-equality of an element and its inverse does NOT imply the element is self-adjoint under the bar-involution; sigma_i is conjugate to sigma_i^-1 (bar-involution sends q->q^-1, sigma_i->sigma_i^-1), so the *centred* element is generally NOT *-fixed. The conclusion may still hold for the trace-moment computation (the proof only needs trace-symmetry, not operator self-adjointness), but as written the implication 'tr equal => self-adjoint' is a false step. Not critical because the downstream moment computations only use trace identities, but the stated lemma is wrong."
      }
